517
00:41:49.633 --> 00:41:51.763
I can... I can go change...

518
00:41:51.927 --> 00:41:55.177
- ...right now.
- No. it's fine.

519
00:41:56.015 --> 00:41:57.925
You look great.

520
00:42:08.527 --> 00:42:10.397
Thank you for staying late.
I appreciate it.

521
00:42:10.571 --> 00:42:13.871
- Thank you. Thanks.
- Thank you.

522
00:42:46.774 --> 00:42:49.324
Well. no one fell in the pool.

523
00:42:49.485 --> 00:42:50.895
The rain stayed away.

524
00:42:51.946 --> 00:42:54.106
I'd call that a win.

525
00:42:54.323 --> 00:42:56.333
I found it in your record collection.

526
00:43:00.579 --> 00:43:02.459
Where's Laura?

527
00:43:02.623 --> 00:43:05.043
Oh. yeah. she crashed about an hour ago.

528
00:43:05.251 --> 00:43:07.841
Has to catch a flight
at 6 in the morning for work.

529
00:43:08.003 --> 00:43:09.843
So how'd our little story hold up?

530
00:43:12.007 --> 00:43:14.297
It was great.

531
00:43:14.468 --> 00:43:16.468
I was acting out a part.

532
00:43:17.263 --> 00:43:20.223
I had a secret in me that no one knew.

533
00:43:22.059 --> 00:43:23.139
Except you.

534
00:43:25.354 --> 00:43:27.024
You know everybody loves you?

535
00:43:27.439 --> 00:43:30.399
- Shut up.
- I'm serious.

536
00:43:30.776 --> 00:43:34.196
It made me think that I made
a good choice for the baby.

537
00:43:35.739 --> 00:43:38.409
Well. I thought that we were
the ones that made the choice.

538
00:43:38.742 --> 00:43:40.202
I could've said no.

539
00:43:40.828 --> 00:43:42.198
True.

540
00:43:43.706 --> 00:43:45.826
You're gonna make a great dad.

541
00:43:47.459 --> 00:43:50.879
Well. I'm glad it was you.

542
00:43:58.721 --> 00:44:03.271
I am gonna take a bath before bed.

543
00:44:09.106 --> 00:44:12.066
Thank you for everything. John.

544
00:44:52.149 --> 00:44:53.649
Is everything okay?

545
00:44:54.109 --> 00:44:56.989
Something's knocking
against the guest house.

546
00:46:42.593 --> 00:46:44.553
Is there coffee?

547
00:46:47.514 --> 00:46:48.684
Yeah. Coming right up.

548
00:46:50.058 --> 00:46:51.638
When does Laura get home?

549
00:46:51.852 --> 00:46:53.652
Tuesday.

550
00:46:58.859 --> 00:47:00.859
So. look. about last night...

551
00:47:07.576 --> 00:47:09.196
Todd Decker. he was...

552
00:47:09.369 --> 00:47:10.659
He was asking about you.

553
00:47:11.580 --> 00:47:16.040
The guy in the Grey suit? You know.
he was staring at me all night.

554
00:47:16.210 --> 00:47:17.840
Had to be uncomfortable for you.

555
00:47:18.795 --> 00:47:21.215
Can't blame a person for staring.

556
00:47:21.381 --> 00:47:24.221
It just means they like what they see.

557
00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:28.310
Actually. I prefer older guys.

558
00:47:29.264 --> 00:47:30.564
I always have.

559
00:47:30.724 --> 00:47:33.394
Mike was the youngest guy I ever dated.

560
00:47:33.560 --> 00:47:36.730
- Is that your phone?
- They'll leave a message.

561
00:47:38.398 --> 00:47:40.068
So I have to go into the office today.

562
00:47:40.234 --> 00:47:41.614
- On a Sunday?
- Yeah.

563
00:47:41.777 --> 00:47:44.567
I got an important deposition.
You can order out.

564
00:47:44.738 --> 00:47:46.158
I'm not gonna be back until late.

565
00:47:56.959 --> 00:47:59.629
How about we go out to the lake house?

566
00:47:59.795 --> 00:48:02.205
Just you and I. a weekend
before the baby comes.

567
00:48:02.381 --> 00:48:04.221
As soon as you get back from Houston.

568
00:48:04.383 --> 00:48:05.763
I'd like that.

569
00:48:05.926 --> 00:48:08.046
John. you're not gonna like this...

570
00:48:08.220 --> 00:48:10.430
...but Chef Folse wants me out here
tomorrow as well.

571
00:48:11.765 --> 00:48:14.725
- You're right. I don't like it.
- Should I say no?

572
00:48:15.269 --> 00:48:17.439
Should I just come home now?

573
00:48:18.021 --> 00:48:20.441
No. go ahead and stay. It's okay.

574
00:48:25.028 --> 00:48:28.118
- Hey.
- I hope you're sitting down.

575
00:48:29.116 --> 00:48:32.866
Chef Folse is offering me
a major promotion.

576
00:48:33.036 --> 00:48:34.036
Really?

577
00:48:34.204 --> 00:48:36.584
That's the reason he brought me down.
so he could offer me...

578
00:48:36.748 --> 00:48:39.708
- ...the CEO position.
- Congratulations.

579
00:48:42.254 --> 00:48:43.844
But I thought we talked about. you know...

580
00:48:44.006 --> 00:48:45.836
We have six months before the baby's born.

581
00:48:46.008 --> 00:48:49.298
I told him I could run the company while
we look for a permanent replacement.

582
00:48:49.469 --> 00:48:50.849
Why not just turn it down. sweetheart?

583
00:48:51.013 --> 00:48:52.063
I think I should take it...

584
00:48:52.222 --> 00:48:55.142
...even if it is only for six months.
But that's assuming you agree.

585
00:48:55.476 --> 00:48:57.806
I mean. I'd have to spend
a few days a month up here.

586
00:48:57.978 --> 00:48:59.728
But that wouldn't be
until later in the year.

587
00:48:59.896 --> 00:49:01.566
And you could come up for some weekends.

588
00:49:02.399 --> 00:49:03.819
Babe. are you happy for me?

589
00:49:03.984 --> 00:49:07.204
- I really wanna do this.
- Yeah. no. sweetheart. Definitely.

590
00:49:07.362 --> 00:49:09.532
I'm... I'm definitely happy for you.

591
00:49:09.740 --> 00:49:10.950
- It's unbelievable.
- Yeah?

592
00:49:11.116 --> 00:49:13.576
And you like spending time
with Anna. right?

593
00:49:15.162 --> 00:49:17.662
She might even have
a little thing for you.

594
00:49:17.873 --> 00:49:19.373
It's cute. Whatever.

595
00:49:19.541 --> 00:49:21.881
I mean. you're a big boy.
you can handle a little attention.

596
00:49:22.044 --> 00:49:24.054
Just congratulate me.

597
00:49:25.672 --> 00:49:27.802
- Jesus. What the...?
- What?

598
00:49:27.966 --> 00:49:31.796
No. congratulations. sweetheart.
I am so proud of you.

599
00:49:33.138 --> 00:49:34.138
I love you.

600
00:49:34.681 --> 00:49:36.311
I'll see you tomorrow.

601
00:49:36.475 --> 00:49:38.475
I love you too. babe.

602
00:51:04.229 --> 00:51:05.899
Anna!

603
00:51:07.482 --> 00:51:10.112
- Hi. John.
- What are you doing?

604
00:51:11.695 --> 00:51:12.945
Look. do you see this?

605
00:51:13.113 --> 00:51:14.873
This is me and Laura.
She is my wife. okay?

606
00:51:15.031 --> 00:51:18.541
This is our home.
Do you not understand that?

607
00:51:19.077 --> 00:51:20.827
I don't wanna have to say anything to her.

608
00:51:21.455 --> 00:51:23.995
Maybe I should go.

609
00:51:24.166 --> 00:51:27.376
No. wait. hold on. No. no. Please. please.

610
00:51:27.544 --> 00:51:29.634
Okay. look.

611
00:51:29.796 --> 00:51:34.256
Maybe... Maybe I said something
to encourage you in all this.

612
00:51:34.426 --> 00:51:36.846
And if I did do that. then I am sorry.

613
00:51:38.764 --> 00:51:40.394
Hello!

614
00:51:40.557 --> 00:51:43.557
- Hey.
- Hi.

615
00:51:43.727 --> 00:51:46.227
Didn't wanna wait until tomorrow.
so I grabbed the next flight.

616
00:51:46.396 --> 00:51:49.606
Good. That's... That's good.
Congratulations on everything.

617
00:51:49.775 --> 00:51:51.565
Hello. Laura.

618
00:51:56.656 --> 00:51:59.986
Laura just got a promotion at her company.

619
00:52:01.661 --> 00:52:04.041
Well. it's only until the baby comes.

620
00:52:04.206 --> 00:52:06.666
- How are you?
- Everything is fine.

621
00:52:07.834 --> 00:52:11.924
- Welcome home.
- It's good to be back.

622
00:52:12.088 --> 00:52:13.298
It's good to have you back.

623
00:52:50.460 --> 00:52:52.250
Hey. baby.

624
00:53:09.729 --> 00:53:10.729
Is anybody home?

625
00:53:13.233 --> 00:53:15.243
Anybody wanna make me a goddamn quiche?

626
00:53:15.402 --> 00:53:17.072
Mike. stop it!

627
00:53:19.364 --> 00:53:22.584
You're drunk. Okay? I was gonna call you.

628
00:53:25.912 --> 00:53:29.082
Before they find out
this whole thing's a scam...

629
00:53:29.291 --> 00:53:31.921
...you're gonna tell them
that you changed your mind.

630
00:53:32.085 --> 00:53:33.795
- You'll get them to give you money.
- No.

631
00:53:33.962 --> 00:53:35.712
Shut up!

632
00:53:37.090 --> 00:53:39.430
You're gonna take that money.

633
00:53:40.135 --> 00:53:43.755
And you and I are heading to Arizona...

634
00:53:44.139 --> 00:53:46.059
...because there is a guy there...

635
00:53:46.224 --> 00:53:49.024
...that's gonna give us another $15.000...

636
00:53:49.185 --> 00:53:54.065
...for a nice. new baby.

637
00:53:59.321 --> 00:54:01.071
If you don't...

638
00:54:01.907 --> 00:54:03.617
...I'm gonna come back here later...

639
00:54:04.492 --> 00:54:08.462
...and I'm gonna tell Laura and John...

640
00:54:08.622 --> 00:54:10.462
...you wanted to take
their last baby from them.

641
00:54:10.999 --> 00:54:12.459
No.

642
00:54:12.626 --> 00:54:14.036
They'll hate you.

643
00:54:20.592 --> 00:54:22.552
Clean this up.

644
00:54:54.417 --> 00:54:56.167
Here you go.

645
00:55:20.986 --> 00:55:21.986
Hey! Hey!

646
00:55:22.529 --> 00:55:25.239
Get... Get back here!

647
00:55:39.462 --> 00:55:42.302
Leave a message
and I'll call you right back.

648
00:55:42.465 --> 00:55:44.175
God.

649
00:55:44.342 --> 00:55:47.052
It's so goddamn typical of you.

650
00:55:47.220 --> 00:55:49.560
Some asshole buys you some fancy shit...

651
00:55:49.723 --> 00:55:52.183
...and you fall head over heels for him.

652
00:55:52.350 --> 00:55:54.230
Call me.

653
00:55:55.937 --> 00:55:58.727
Stupid bitch.

654
00:56:49.866 --> 00:56:51.446
Yeah.

655
00:56:52.494 --> 00:56:54.374
You're the brains. Mike.

656
00:57:15.225 --> 00:57:18.685
I am happy.

657
00:57:20.021 --> 00:57:23.441
I am in control...

658
00:57:23.608 --> 00:57:25.938
...of my life.

659
00:57:26.736 --> 00:57:30.696
I feel the joy...

660
00:57:30.865 --> 00:57:33.905
...of pure love.

661
00:57:51.386 --> 00:57:54.426
Hi. this is Laura Taylor.
Leave a message. and I'll...

662
00:57:57.642 --> 00:57:59.232
I can't hold the room. I'm sorry.

663
00:58:00.145 --> 00:58:01.895
You know what. let's just go ahead and...

664
00:58:02.605 --> 00:58:04.315
- Should we?
- I...

665
00:58:04.482 --> 00:58:05.902
- Okay. All right.
- I left a message.

666
00:58:07.110 --> 00:58:09.200
That's the femur.

667
00:58:10.321 --> 00:58:12.661
It's a boy.

668
00:58:13.366 --> 00:58:14.576
I told you.

669
00:58:15.243 --> 00:58:16.623
She's right.

670
00:58:16.786 --> 00:58:18.536
That's definitely a boy.

671
00:58:22.667 --> 00:58:25.457
Honey. No. wait.

672
00:58:25.628 --> 00:58:27.378
It's a boy.

673
00:58:28.339 --> 00:58:29.509
- It's a boy.
- No. babe...

674
00:58:29.674 --> 00:58:31.974
...just get down here as soon as you can.

675
00:58:33.553 --> 00:58:35.513
That's my son.

676
00:58:37.098 --> 00:58:38.598
I'm looking at my son.

677
00:58:43.855 --> 00:58:46.015
Look at his head.

678
00:58:47.650 --> 00:58:49.530
That's my son.

679
00:58:49.736 --> 00:58:52.106
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

680
00:59:00.246 --> 00:59:02.496
I'm sorry. I had it in my schedule
as 2:00.

681
00:59:02.665 --> 00:59:06.035
- Maybe you just entered it wrong.
- No. I didn't enter it wrong. I...

682
00:59:06.211 --> 00:59:07.751
Damn it. I know I didn't. I... I...

683
00:59:07.921 --> 00:59:11.591
Someone changed it in my phone!
I know that I put it in right.

684
00:59:11.758 --> 00:59:14.798
I booked my flights around it!
I know that I did! Damn it!

685
00:59:14.969 --> 00:59:17.059
- I... I...
- Laura. Stop it. Please.

686
00:59:18.431 --> 00:59:19.681
Please.

687
00:59:21.893 --> 00:59:26.483
This is the only time
we're ever gonna be able to do this.

688
00:59:26.648 --> 00:59:29.898
It's all right. Just don't worry about it.

689
00:59:38.826 --> 00:59:42.116
Let's just go somewhere.
I don't know. lunch.

690
00:59:45.250 --> 00:59:47.130
I can't.

691
00:59:47.961 --> 00:59:51.011
I left a client at the airport.

692
00:59:52.090 --> 00:59:54.340
I have to go back.

693
01:00:10.942 --> 01:00:12.532
Anna Walsh on 2.

694
01:00:12.694 --> 01:00:13.744
Hello?

695
01:00:13.903 --> 01:00:17.453
I'm so excited. A boy.

696
01:00:17.615 --> 01:00:21.325
I knew it. Let's have lunch today.
To celebrate.

697
01:00:21.536 --> 01:00:23.746
Just you and me. I promise it'll be fun.

698
01:00:23.913 --> 01:00:25.833
- Anna. is there anything actually wrong?
- Why?

699
01:00:25.999 --> 01:00:27.709
Because you shouldn't
be calling me at work.

700
01:00:27.917 --> 01:00:30.457
Okay? I cannot sneak away.
I will not have lunch with you.

701
01:00:30.670 --> 01:00:33.340
I have appointments all afternoon.
Like I said earlier...

702
01:00:39.971 --> 01:00:43.521
Mr. Taylor's office. Please hold.

703
01:00:44.183 --> 01:00:47.233
- Anna Walsh.
- Tell her I left for the day.

704
01:00:56.779 --> 01:00:59.909
- What is it?
- Why are you lying to me?

705
01:01:00.491 --> 01:01:02.201
What are you talking about?

706
01:01:02.368 --> 01:01:05.158
I'd never lie to you. John.

707
01:01:06.205 --> 01:01:09.165
I've always told you the truth.

708
01:01:10.043 --> 01:01:12.093
But not you.

709
01:01:12.462 --> 01:01:13.502
Why are you saying that?

710
01:01:13.671 --> 01:01:16.051
Because I'm right here.

711
01:01:28.519 --> 01:01:30.649
This is for you.

712
01:01:31.147 --> 01:01:33.477
A congratulations.

713
01:01:34.442 --> 01:01:36.492
All right. No. we're not gonna do this.

714
01:01:36.652 --> 01:01:39.322
We're not gonna do this.

715
01:01:39.906 --> 01:01:41.276
Let's do something fun.

716
01:01:44.535 --> 01:01:48.785
Nope. We're not doing anything fun.

717
01:01:55.254 --> 01:01:58.304
What a surprise.
Laura's working late again!

718
01:01:58.466 --> 01:02:00.296
Why did you think
she would make a good mother?

719
01:02:00.468 --> 01:02:03.008
- Enough!
- We're so different.

720
01:02:03.221 --> 01:02:04.851
She couldn't even stay pregnant.

721
01:02:05.014 --> 01:02:07.024
I wonder if she actually even wanted to.

722
01:02:07.225 --> 01:02:08.635
Are you sure she had miscarriages?

723
01:02:08.810 --> 01:02:11.400
Because you know there are ways
to fake that. right?

724
01:02:11.562 --> 01:02:15.532
- Are you out of your mind?
- You need to be nicer to me. John.

725
01:02:15.691 --> 01:02:18.151
I will leave. The law says I can.

726
01:02:18.319 --> 01:02:22.619
This is my baby. Mike says we can sell it.

727
01:02:26.786 --> 01:02:28.656
- John!
- You know what?

728
01:02:29.789 --> 01:02:31.829
Leave. Go. Get out of the house!

729
01:02:31.999 --> 01:02:34.249
- You don't mean that.
- Oh. yes. I do.

730
01:02:34.460 --> 01:02:37.630
I'll tell Laura everything.
It will kill her. It will break her heart.

731
01:02:37.797 --> 01:02:40.047
But you know what? We'll survive it.

732
01:02:40.383 --> 01:02:43.683
We'll pick up the pieces and move on
because that's what we do.

733
01:02:43.845 --> 01:02:47.135
But what about you? You'll be alone.

734
01:02:47.306 --> 01:02:50.976
You'll be broke.
with a kid that's not even really yours.

735
01:02:51.477 --> 01:02:53.187
So go for it.

736
01:02:53.354 --> 01:02:55.194
Leave.

737
01:03:00.403 --> 01:03:02.953
I just want you.

738
01:03:25.052 --> 01:03:27.432
- White here.
- Hey. Roland. it's John.

739
01:03:27.597 --> 01:03:30.927
Hey. what's up? What. the old man
needs another rock looked under?

740
01:03:31.142 --> 01:03:34.102
No. actually. I need a favour.
And it's not business.

741
01:03:34.312 --> 01:03:35.902
- It's personal.
- Sure. John.

742
01:03:36.856 --> 01:03:39.686
There's a guy I'd like you to look into.
His name is Mike Mitchell.

743
01:03:39.859 --> 01:03:41.819
He's Navy. based in Louisiana.

744
01:03:41.986 --> 01:03:44.736
He's been deployed about two months.
Just need a history on him.

745
01:03:44.906 --> 01:03:47.156
Anything you can find would be great.

746
01:03:47.325 --> 01:03:50.235
I'm on it. Anything for you. John.

747
01:03:50.411 --> 01:03:51.911
My man.

748
01:04:04.425 --> 01:04:05.465
You wanted to see me?

749
01:04:06.511 --> 01:04:07.551
Have a seat. John.

750
01:04:14.101 --> 01:04:17.561
Look. you know
the firm monitors computer use...

751
01:04:17.730 --> 01:04:19.360
...and e-mail accounts.

752
01:04:19.524 --> 01:04:21.824
The system's set up
to automatically snag...

753
01:04:21.984 --> 01:04:24.824
...certain types of files.
things that could...

754
01:04:25.655 --> 01:04:28.065
...embarrass the company.

755
01:04:47.885 --> 01:04:51.555
Todd recognised her from your party.

756
01:04:51.722 --> 01:04:53.722
She's not your relative. is she?

757
01:04:53.891 --> 01:04:56.891
No. She's our surrogate.

758
01:04:57.061 --> 01:04:58.981
And I don't see
how this is company business.

759
01:04:59.146 --> 01:05:01.436
Anna has been getting
prenatal care from a clinic...

760
01:05:01.607 --> 01:05:03.897
...that happens to be a subsidiary
of Grafton Industries.

761
01:05:04.068 --> 01:05:06.818
She is a patient of the very people...

762
01:05:06.988 --> 01:05:10.118
...we're about to take to court.

763
01:05:10.408 --> 01:05:13.238
That's a big deal. John.

764
01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:15.620
I'm giving the case to Todd.

765
01:05:16.831 --> 01:05:18.831
I hope you understand.

766
01:05:20.376 --> 01:05:22.876
I'm sorry. John. That video got bounced
straight to the old man.

767
01:05:23.045 --> 01:05:25.335
I think I just lost my job.

768
01:05:27.300 --> 01:05:28.880
You ready for things to get worse?

769
01:05:29.093 --> 01:05:30.803
I don't think that's possible.

770
01:05:30.970 --> 01:05:33.510
Remember that guy you asked me
to run a check on? Mitchell?

771
01:05:35.308 --> 01:05:36.848
- Yeah.
- Two years ago...

772
